description:
FILED s513g (Opus, 2026-10-09); NOT fixed (a runtime I/O bug, outside the overlay batch).  Pre-existing on main b7bf55b9 (the program has no overlay-affected name).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 prints `3`; PCL dies with a Lisp backtrace -- rule 12 and the "errors must be tidy" ruling both):

    use Fcntl;
    my $p = "/tmp/s513g-sk2.txt";
    unlink $p;
    sysopen(my $fh, $p, O_RDWR | O_CREAT | O_EXCL, 0600) or die "sysopen: $!";
    print {$fh} "abc";
    seek $fh, 0, 2 or die "seek: $!";
    print tell($fh), "\n";

PCL: `Unhandled simple-type-error ... #<sb-sys:fd-stream for "/tmp/..."> is not a stream associated with a file.` from `(FILE-LENGTH stream)` called by `PCL::%P-SEEK-IMPL`.  The fd-stream sysopen builds carries a name but no FILE slot, and SBCL's FILE-LENGTH refuses such a stream.  The same with `File::Temp->new` (it sysopens) and with a `>&` dup of that fd (scratch/s513g/pr/sk1.pl).  Fix direction (not designed): SEEK_END takes the size from fstat on the fd (sb-posix:fstat / stat-size), never FILE-LENGTH; check `tell` / `-s` / `eof` on the same handle kind for the same call.

WHAT IT BLOCKS: Capture::Tiny's `_capture_tee` does `seek( $stash->{capture}{$_}, 0, 2 )` (Tiny.pm:361) on its File::Temp capture handles.  Before s513g every `capture { ... }` call was DROPPED at compile time (#1509); with the s513g facts overlay (lib/PCL/Facts/Capture/Tiny.pm) the call compiles and runs, and dies HERE.  So 02-capture / 09-preserve-exit-code / 17-pass-results / 19-relayering / 25-cap-fork all stop on this cause now (the s513g STOP.md has the row-by-row reading).
